    "Transports  - Bordeaux Montaigne University v1.2\nGo to content\nGo to search\nGo to menu\nTransports  - Bordeaux Montaigne University v1.2\nShare\nShare on Facebook\nShare on LinkedIn\nSend by Mail\nYour name\n*\nYour mail\n*\nRecipient(s)\n*\nSeparated by coma\nMessage\nImage's text\n*\nIf the image is not clear enough, you can refresh the page.\nTransportation\nIn the Bordeaux metropolitan area, tram, bus and bike-sharing services are provided by the\nTBM\nnetwork (Transports Bordeaux Métropole). On their website and mobile app, you can find real-time timetables, a personalised route planner, traffic information and maps of the areas connected by TBM.\nYou can find all relevant information on fares and subscriptions ont the TBM's\nonline shop\n.\nHow to get to Bordeaux Montaigne University\nBordeaux Montaigne University is located on the Pessac-Talence-Gradignan campus (6 km from Bordeaux city center).\nYou can get to the university:\nBy\ntramway\n: the\nB line\nruns from 5am to midnight on weekdays (and up to 1am on Thursdays, Fridays and Saturdays), with trams running every 10 minutes on average. The university is located right next to the \"Montaigne-Montesquieu\" tram stop.\nBy\nbus\n: you can get from the train station to Bordeaux Montaigne University on lines\n31 and 35\n. The night line,\nTBNight\n, also serves the campus (Talence, Pessac and Gradignan) on Thursday, Friday and Saturday from 1.30am to 6.30am.\nBy\nbike\n: the TBM network provides more than 2,000 self-service bikes, including 1,000 electric ones. You can also access TBM \"\nvélo'c\n\" bike loan, hire and parking service.\nBy\ncar\n: you can check the rules for the use of foreign licences at\nhttps://www.service-public.fr/particuliers/vosdroits/N19126?lang=en\nUseful information\nAt\nÉtu’Recup\n’s « Maison du vélo », you can buy refurbished bikes at very reasonable prices. The association also offers bike repair workshops, where volunteers and technicians are on hand to help all participants with their diagnostics and repairs. There, you can also find low-cost second-hand parts.\n5\nintercity bus routes\nserve the Talence campus: lines 406, 502, 503, 504 and 505. Bus line 602 (Hôpital Pellegrin - Pieces de Choisy) stops at Bordeaux Montaigne campus (Unitec).\nDepending on your income or circumstances, you may be eligible for the TBM Solidarity Fare scheme, which offers significant discounts (or even free travel) on your travel pass.\nMedias\nInstagram\nBluesky\nScoop.it\nYoutube\nLinkedIn\nSoundCloud\nHelp\nAccessibility: non-compliant\nSitemap\nLegal notice\nContact us\nUniversité Bordeaux Montaigne\nBordeaux Montaigne University\nAccess map\nDomaine Universitaire\nF33607 Pessac Cedex\nContact university\nPartners\nfooter-script"
